{"created": "2026-07-19T04:16:02.248651+00:00", "modified": "2026-07-29T11:30:47.197352+00:00", "id": 21436679, "conceptrecid": "21436678", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21436679", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21436678", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21436679", "metadata": {"title": "Prediction Presupposes Persistence", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21436679", "publication_date": "2026-07-19", "description": "<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\"><strong>Prediction Presupposes Persistence</strong> is a position paper arguing that language is possible only over a persistent world, and that this ordering &mdash; world first, language last &mdash; is an architectural requirement for AI systems, not a philosophical preference.</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">The paper makes one claim and stakes it falsifiably: any system that produces language without a persistent world beneath it will fail precisely where language depends on persistence &mdash; in stable reference across discourse, in identity over time, in reporting absence rather than confabulating referents, and in grounded refusal. Hallucination is analysed as an ontological problem rather than a data or scale problem: in a system with no world, nothing can be false, because there is nothing for a claim to be false <em>against</em>.</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">The argument is situated against the 2025&ndash;2026 industry turn toward world models, which is read as a half-concession: the field has agreed that language requires grounding, but continues to derive existence from prediction &mdash; a world inferred on demand &mdash; where language requires the dependency to run the other way. Five specific failure modes are predicted, including the forecast that every successful mitigation will prove to be a persistence layer under another name.</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">The position described is implemented in Aurora-Lens via the Persistent Existence Frame (PEF), with provenance anchored to November 2025 and documented in the related records listed herein, including an empirical demonstration of the first predicted failure mode (pronoun ambiguity resolution, DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.21124705).</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Stokes, Margaret", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0004-6422-4174"}], "keywords": ["persistent existence", "world models", "language grounding", "reference", "anaphora", "hallucination", "admissibility", "refusal", "AI governance", "ontology", "Aurora-Lens", "PEF"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21397474", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21123912", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.19881958", "relation": "isPartOf", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21436678"}}]}}, "title": "Prediction Presupposes Persistence", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21436679", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21436679?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21436679", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21436679", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21436679", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436678", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21436678", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21436678", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21436678", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21436679/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21436679/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21436679:Prediction_Presupposes_Persistence_Stokes_2026.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21436679:Prediction_Presupposes_Persistence_Stokes_2026.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21436679:Prediction_Presupposes_Persistence_Stokes_2026.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21436679:Prediction_Presupposes_Persistence_Stokes_2026.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21436679:Prediction_Presupposes_Persistence_Stokes_2026.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21436679:Prediction_Presupposes_Persistence_Stokes_2026.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679/files-archive", "archive_media": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679/media-files-archive", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21436679/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21436679/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/214366